Reason:
The bug occurs because the code incorrectly uses the `pudp` pointer, which points to the page upper directory entry, instead of the correct `pmdp` pointer that references the page middle directory entry when setting a 2MB page table entry (PTE). This leads to improper memory mapping, as the wrong pointer type is being cast and used.

